{
  "program": "CBSTM03A",
  "caseId": "case03",
  "description": "The FIRST element of the 1-based 51x10 WS-TRNX-TABLE, pinned through a complete STMTFILE write order that contains two genuine duplications. Two cards are loaded and the cross-reference names the lower one, so the statement is composed from WS-CARD-NUM(1) and WS-TRAN-NUM(1,1) (app/cbl/CBSTM03A.CBL:L226-L230, gate G33); a 0-based read would compose it from the second card's transaction instead, and every 80-byte image below would change. THE WRITE ORDER, WITH BOTH DUPLICATIONS PRESERVED (gate G32, practice B5): 5000-CREATE-STATEMENT writes ST-LINE0 (:460), then 5100-WRITE-HTML-HEADER, then fifteen records at :488-:502 - ST-LINE1, ST-LINE2, ST-LINE3, ST-LINE4, ST-LINE5, ST-LINE6, ST-LINE5 AGAIN at :494, ST-LINE7, ST-LINE8, ST-LINE9, ST-LINE10, ST-LINE11, ST-LINE12, ST-LINE13, ST-LINE12 AGAIN at :502 - then one ST-LINE14 per transaction (:679), then ST-LINE12 a THIRD time, ST-LINE14A and ST-LINE15 (:435-:437). ST-LINE5 is therefore written twice and ST-LINE12 three times, which with ST-LINE10 puts a byte-identical 80-dash rule at zero-based write positions 5, 7, 11, 13, 15 and 16+N: the three items are distinguished by POSITION, never by content. The repeats are the COBOL's own and are reproduced verbatim - de-duplicating one, reordering one or 'optimising' the block lowers the row count and shifts every following index, which is a parity violation and not a cleanup. With N = 1 the sequence is exactly 19 + N = 20 records at contiguous zero-based positions, and HTMLFILE is 64 + 11N = 75 - 22 from 5100-WRITE-HTML-HEADER (:509-:552), 34 from 5200-WRITE-HTML-NMADBS (:568-:669), 11 per transaction (:682-:721) and the 8-record footer (:440-:454); expectedDatasets pins both counts and both widths on the WRITES channel. UNIT AND INVOCATION: statement.StatementGenerationJobA as a BATCH_JOB, reached at step/Tasklet level with statement.StatementGenerationJobB as its constructor-injected collaborator - no JobLauncher, no job repository and no HTTP in the path (gate G51). jobParameters is empty because app/jcl/CREASTMT.JCL declares no PARM on any of its five steps; of those five only STEP020 (:56), STEP030 (:66) and STEP040 (:79) carry COND=(0,NE), and STEP040 runs this program. No abend arm is reached, so expectedReturnCode is 0. EVERY LINE TEMPLATE SUMS TO EXACTLY 80 (practice B11, gates G19 and G21), by addition of its PICTURE widths: ST-LINE0 31+18+31; ST-LINE1 75+5; ST-LINE2 and ST-LINE3 50+30; ST-LINE4 80; ST-LINE5, ST-LINE10 and ST-LINE12 a single X(80); ST-LINE6 33+14+33; ST-LINE7 and ST-LINE9 20+20+40; ST-LINE8 20+13+7+40; ST-LINE11 30+20+30; ST-LINE13 16+51+13; ST-LINE14 16+1+49+1+13; ST-LINE14A 10+56+1+13; ST-LINE15 32+16+32 - seventeen items in all, ST-LINE0 through ST-LINE15 plus ST-LINE14A (:85-:146). WIDTHS COME FROM TWO SOURCES EACH: STMTFILE is 80 bytes, from 01 FD-STMTFILE-REC PIC X(80) (:45) and from CREASTMT.JCL LINE 89, DCB=(LRECL=80,BLKSIZE=8000,RECFM=FB), under the STMTFILE DD at line 87. Line 90 of that JCL is genuinely corrupted - verbatim '//         SPACE=(CYL,(1,1),RLSE), 00,RECFM=FB), ATA.VSAM.KSDS', a text-overlay artefact - and its ' 00,RECFM=FB)' remnant sits directly beneath STMTFILE where it is easily misread as LRECL=100. Line 89 is authoritative, and the JCL is left exactly as it stands: it is the parity oracle, so the hazard is recorded and worked around here rather than corrected there (practice B4). HTMLFILE is 100 bytes, from 01 FD-HTMLFILE-REC PIC X(100) (:47) and from line 94, DCB=(LRECL=100,BLKSIZE=800,RECFM=FB), which supersedes STEP030's pre-delete LRECL=80,BLKSIZE=3200 at line 69 because the step that creates the dataset wins (gate G20, risk R-G). FIELD GRANULARITY: both FD records are single elementary items, and the 20 STMTFILE records are 20 different line templates that no one multi-span layout could honestly describe, so exactly one addressable span is declared per dataset - FD-STMTFILE-REC and FD-HTMLFILE-REC. Each expectation pins that span by its whole image, which parity.FieldDiffer walks span by span rather than comparing as one opaque string, and which at the same time fixes the total width and so proves that every VALUE SPACES and FILLER span was emitted. EDIT MASKS, EXACTLY: ST-CURR-BAL PIC 9(9).99- is NOT zero-suppressed, so ACCT-CURR-BAL +492.00 renders '000000492.00 ' with its leading zeros intact; ST-TRANAMT and ST-TOTAL-TRAMT PIC Z(9).99- ARE zero-suppressed, so 11.11 renders '      11.11 ' - 13 bytes each, 9 digit positions plus '.' plus 2 plus a trailing sign position that is blank for a positive value and '-' for a negative one. ARITHMETIC AT SCALE 2, TRUNCATING: WS-TOTAL-AMT PIC S9(9)V99 COMP-3 (:64-:65) and WS-TRN-AMT PIC S9(9)V99 (:68) are both scale 2, and ADD TRNX-AMT TO WS-TOTAL-AMT (:429) is the only arithmetic on this path; every amount is a BigDecimal at scale 2 with RoundingMode.DOWN - never HALF_UP, never HALF_EVEN, never double and never float - because ROUNDED appears zero times in all 28 programs. The chosen card's TRNX-AMT '0000000111A' is an 11-byte zoned S9(09)V99 closing on the +1 overpunch, so 11.11, and it is the ONLY transaction summed: the second card's '0000000999I' is never reached, which is what makes the 1-based selection observable in ST-LINE14 and in the Total EXP line at once. SEEDS ARE REAL BYTES: XREFFILE is row 0 of app/data/ASCII/cardxref.txt verbatim - XREF-CARD-NUM 0500024453765740, XREF-CUST-ID 000000050, XREF-ACCT-ID 00000000050 - and it stays 36 bytes here; ParityCase.Normalisation is the sole owner of the 14-space pad up to CVACT03Y's declared 50 and applies it once, at seed time, through the declared CARDXREF_FILLER_PAD_36_TO_50, so the fixture is never edited and the pad is never double-applied (gate G16). ACCTFILE and CUSTFILE are acctdata.txt (300 x 50) and custdata.txt (500 x 50) whole, and the customer is read through CUSTREC, whose date of birth is CUST-DOB-YYYYMMDD and never CVCUS01Y's CUST-DOB-YYYY-MM-DD. TRNXFILE IS INLINE BECAUSE THERE IS NO TENTH FIXTURE: app/data/ASCII holds exactly nine .txt files and none is a statement transaction file, so both rows are composed from app/cpy/COSTM01.CPY at exactly 350 bytes - TRNX-CARD-NUM X(16) plus TRNX-ID X(16) as the 32-byte composite key that DELDEF01's IDCAMS corroborates with KEYS(32 0) at :30 and RECORDSIZE(350 350) at :32, then 2+4+10+100+11+9+50+50+10+26+26 = 298 plus a trailing FILLER X(20) emitted as spaces = 318 - and they are ordered ascending by card then id, the order STEP010's SORT FIELDS=(263,16,CH,A,1,16,CH,A) with OUTREC FIELDS=(1:263,16,17:1,262,279:279,50) (:53-:54) produces. MESSAGES: the nine DISPLAY_LINE expectations are the TIOT walk and nothing else - the job and step line at :270, the 'DD Names from TIOT: ' line at :275, one ' -- valid UCB' line at :279 for each of STEP040's six dataset DDs in JCL declaration order (:83-:92), and the post-loop entry at :290 whose ' -- null  UCB' is byte-different from the in-loop ' --  null UCB' at :281. DETERMINISM: nothing here is read from a clock; TRNX-ORIG-TS and TRNX-PROC-TS are seed bytes carrying the fixed 2022-07-18 12:00:00.000000 literal the shipped data uses, never a 'now'. Bytes are US-ASCII throughout, matching app/data/ASCII, and never a platform default. PROVENANCE: every expected value here is STATICALLY DERIVED - by structured reading of the CBSTM03A paragraphs, cross-checked against the COSTM01, CUSTREC, CVACT01Y and CVACT03Y byte layouts, the CREASTMT.JCL DD and DCB contracts and the real ASCII fixtures. It was never captured from, recorded against or replayed from any execution of the legacy COBOL, which is empirically impossible in this environment: there is no z/OS or CICS runtime, the available compiler reports its indexed file handler disabled, no Language Environment CEE* services exist, and app/cpy/CUSTREC.cpy carries literal TAB characters that break parsing outright. WHAT THE RUN LEAVES BEHIND, OBSERVED RATHER THAN ASKED ABOUT: app/jcl/CREASTMT.JCL:L87-L96 declares both outputs DISP=(NEW,CATLG,DELETE), so a run that reaches 9999-GOBACK retains exactly the records it wrote and a run that does not retains none of them. Both datasets are opened on every path that runs at all, which makes both observable on every such path, so this case declares a FINAL_STATE expectation for each - byte for byte, and identical to its WRITES channel because this run completes with RETURN-CODE 0. It is declared unconditionally rather than only for the cases whose adapter chose to look: an observation selected by consulting the expectation makes the two sides of the comparison one side, and a case that ought to have pinned a retained record but did not would have had nothing observed to contradict it.",
